lib/srv-data-fs/srvdata.img via /etc/fstab with the uquota option) owned by datauser, with an XFS user quota of 100MB soft/hard set via xfs_quota. Enforcement is filesystem-native (kernel EDQUOT, not a wrapper script) and was verified both before and after a full node reboot, confirming the mount/quota configuration persists via fstab and continues enforcing the 100MB cap post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1: root fs is XFS mounted noquota with no spare block device, so created a dedicated loop-backed 2G XFS image for /srv/data instead of altering root fs mount options\",\"Created local user 'datauser' on node1\",\"Created /var/lib/srv-data-fs/srvdata.img, formatted as XFS, added fstab entry '/var/lib/srv-data-fs/srvdata.img /srv/data xfs loop,uquota 0 0', mounted it\",\"chowned /srv/data to datauser and set xfs_quota limit bsoft=100m bhard=100m for datauser\",\"Verified enforcement pre-reboot: writes up to 100MB succeed, next write fails with 'Disk quota exceeded' at exactly the 100MB boundary; cleaned up test files\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and quota state on node1, issued a background 'systemctl reboot' whose acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again; confirmed boot_id changed and fresh uptime, proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Post-reboot verified /srv/data mount, ownership, and xfs_quota state/report persisted automatically via fstab\",\"Re-ran a 150MB write test live post-reboot to confirm the kernel still enforces the 100MB cap after restart; cleaned up test file, leaving /srv/data empty with quota at 0 used / 100M limit\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"datauser account created on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-afea6709b03f4965\"],\"summary\":\"useradd -m datauser succeeded; id shows uid=1000(datauser)\"},{\"requirement\":\"/srv/data set up as a filesystem-enforced quota target (dedicated XFS mount with usrquota)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3a052e0ee6f944a5\",\"cmd-1bead3b1b05f4e78\"],\"summary\":\"Created and formatted XFS loop image, added fstab entry with uquota option, mounted at /srv/data; mount output shows 'type xfs (...,usrquota)'\"},{\"requirement\":\"100MB quota limit applied to datauser on /srv/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-612aba2b5782422a\"],\"summary\":\"xfs_quota limit set bsoft=100m bhard=100m for datauser; report confirms 100M/100M soft/hard for datauser\"},{\"requirement\":\"Quota is enforced by the filesystem itself (kernel-level EDQUOT), not merely configured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-716ef7bff93a4533\"],\"summary\":\"datauser dd write of 80MB succeeded, second 80MB write failed mid-stream with 'Disk quota exceeded' at the 100MB boundary; xfs_quota report shows Used=100M\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline: boot identity and quota-enforcing mount state captured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-25f8845dd5334145\",\"cmd-b49fddfbb27f4538\"],\"summary\":\"Test files cleaned (quota back to 0 used); boot_id 434803ac-a01f-4272-ba59-a0cdb0c4dd92 captured; mount and 'xfs_quota state -u' both show usrquota Accounting/Enforcement ON\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7254b081475e4b4c\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'systemctl reboot' via nohup/disown returned 'reboot scheduled' before the node dropped\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node actually restarted (changed boot identity), not just time elapsed\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1777a8581cbf4b06\",\"cmd-349c4c8e992e4b02\",\"cmd-c79ac08d65d84df2\",\"cmd-764b1fce58294910\"],\"summary\":\"Connection timed out/reset during reboot window, then exec succeeded again with new boot_id afd84d52-7891-42f8-94ad-0c3dd704c4ef (differs from baseline) and uptime '0 min', proving a real reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery: quota-enforced mount, ownership, and limits persisted and are still live\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-efb3ee600d324f5d\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, /srv/data still mounted xfs with usrquota, owned by datauser:datauser, and xfs_quota report/state show Accounting/Enforcement ON with datauser limit still 100M/100M\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart proof the 100MB limit is still actively enforced by the filesystem (not just config)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dc0f73eadc0b4989\",\"cmd-0a0ef6ab6de04483\"],\"summary\":\"Live post-reboot write of 150MB stopped exactly at 100MB with 'Disk quota exceeded'; test file removed and /srv/data verified empty with quota reset to 0 used / 100M limit\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, /srv/data is now a dedicated XFS filesystem (loop-mounted from /var/lib/srv-data-fs/srvdata.img via /etc/fstab with the uquota option) owned by datauser, with an XFS user quota of 100MB soft/hard set via xfs_quota. Enforcement is filesystem-native (kernel EDQUOT, not a wrapper script) and was verified both before and after a full node reboot, confirming the mount/quota configuration persists via fstab and continues enforcing the 100MB cap post-restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1: root fs is XFS mounted noquota with no spare block device, so created a dedicated loop-backed 2G XFS image for /srv/data instead of altering root fs mount options","Created local user 'datauser' on node1","Created /var/lib/srv-data-fs/srvdata.img, formatted as XFS, added fstab entry '/var/lib/srv-data-fs/srvdata.img /srv/data xfs loop,uquota 0 0', mounted it","chowned /srv/data to datauser and set xfs_quota limit bsoft=100m bhard=100m for datauser","Verified enforcement pre-reboot: writes up to 100MB succeed, next write fails with 'Disk quota exceeded' at exactly the 100MB boundary; cleaned up test files","Captured baseline boot_id and quota state on node1, issued a background 'systemctl reboot' whose acknowledgement returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec was available again; confirmed boot_id changed and fresh uptime, proving an actual restart occurred","Post-reboot verified /srv/data mount, ownership, and xfs_quota state/report persisted automatically via fstab","Re-ran a 150MB write test live post-reboot to confirm the kernel still enforces the 100MB cap after restart; cleaned up test file, leaving /srv/data empty with quota at 0 used / 100M limit"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"datauser account created on node1","command_ids":["cmd-afea6709b03f4965"],"summary":"useradd -m datauser succeeded; id shows uid=1000(datauser)"},{"requirement":"/srv/data set up as a filesystem-enforced quota target (dedicated XFS mount with usrquota)","command_ids":["cmd-3a052e0ee6f944a5","cmd-1bead3b1b05f4e78"],"summary":"Created and formatted XFS loop image, added fstab entry with uquota option, mounted at /srv/data; mount output shows 'type xfs (...,usrquota)'"},{"requirement":"100MB quota limit applied to datauser on /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-612aba2b5782422a"],"summary":"xfs_quota limit set bsoft=100m bhard=100m for datauser; report confirms 100M/100M soft/hard for datauser"},{"requirement":"Quota is enforced by the filesystem itself (kernel-level EDQUOT), not merely configured","command_ids":["cmd-716ef7bff93a4533"],"summary":"datauser dd write of 80MB succeeded, second 80MB write failed mid-stream with 'Disk quota exceeded' at the 100MB boundary; xfs_quota report shows Used=100M"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline: boot identity and quota-enforcing mount state captured","command_ids":["cmd-25f8845dd5334145","cmd-b49fddfbb27f4538"],"summary":"Test files cleaned (quota back to 0 used); boot_id 434803ac-a01f-4272-ba59-a0cdb0c4dd92 captured; mount and 'xfs_quota state -u' both show usrquota Accounting/Enforcement ON"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection","command_ids":["cmd-7254b081475e4b4c"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'systemctl reboot' via nohup/disown returned 'reboot scheduled' before the node dropped"},{"requirement":"Node actually restarted (changed boot identity), not just time elapsed","command_ids":["cmd-1777a8581cbf4b06","cmd-349c4c8e992e4b02","cmd